dwg2pdf 0.5.2 / GUI 0.2.21 -- COMPLETE release, 2026-10-06
================================================================

Everything needed to run, test and rebuild. Nothing omitted.

  dwg2pdf.py                 engine, revision 0.5.2
  dwg2pdf_gui.py             Qt GUI (qtpy -> PySide6), revision 0.2.21
  test_autocad.py            186 checks, runs anywhere
  test_gui.py                 91 checks (+2 skipped without a DWG decoder),
                             needs a Qt platform
  test_images.py              21 checks
  make_test_drawings.py      generates test_drawings/ and test_images/
  README.md                  the whole record, including section 9
  environment-dwg2pdf.yml    mamba/conda environment
  build_libredwg.sh          rebuilds the bundled decoder from source
  vendor/libredwg-win64/     LibreDWG 0.14.8593, Windows x86-64 (GPL-3)
  dwg_samples/               real DWGs, five source versions
  docs/                      screenshots referenced by the README

NOT BUNDLED: ODA File Converter.  It is proprietary, ODA do not distribute
it as a redistributable component, and for ODA non-members it is licensed
for NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY.  Point --oda-exe (or the GUI's "ODA File
Converter" field) at your own installation.  Its absence is never an error.

0.5.2 -- WHAT THIS FIXES
------------------------
The accoreconsole -PLOT driver was desynchronised in TWO places, and
neither was the plot device name:

  1. the setup burst fed FILEDIA/CMDDIA/BACKGROUNDPLOT and -PLOT in one
     go, so the "Enter new value for X" prompts it generated were matched
     against the -PLOT answer table, missed, and were each answered with a
     BARE NEWLINE that later shifted every plot answer by one;

  2. a prompt was recognised by a trailing ":" OR ">", and the console is
     read one byte at a time, so "<Model>" fired the test BEFORE the colon
     arrived -- the prompt was read twice and the phantom second read got
     another stray newline.

Every accoreconsole attempt failed for these reasons, including all 20
plot-device calibration candidates at 60 s each.

VERIFIED HERE / NOT VERIFIED HERE
---------------------------------
Verified by the suites below on this build: the phase machine against a
simulated console replaying the field transcript (plus a control that
replays the 0.5.1 order and asserts it still FAILS), worker logging under
a forced spawn, CLI/GUI parity across all 50 options, settings coverage
for the spawn boundary, raw docstrings, the platform guard, and the
layout/extent classification.

NOT verified here -- no AutoCAD on the build host: the phase machine
against real accoreconsole, --acad-device, --acad-probe-timeout and the
system-variable restore.  Those are unit-tested only.  Treat the first
real run as the test.

